<!-- Trailer: a clapperboard, not a screen.

     The previous mark was a 16:9 frame with the play triangle inside it, and
     next to the row's real play button it read as a second, quieter play
     button - a plain box around a small triangle says nothing about a
     trailer. The slate is the one shape that says "preview" on its own, and
     it is still built the way everything else on this row is (see
     ic_detail_shuffle): 24x24 viewport, 2.2-unit bars, the same isoceles
     triangle for any mark that points.

     The lid is the board's own top bar, split into two teeth by a 2.2-unit
     notch - wide enough to survive the 18dp render, where the 1.1-unit
     notches of a three-tooth lid would close up into a solid bar. The board
     is three bars (two sides, one base) around a 12.8 x 10.2 inner area, and
     the play mark inside is the square-sided triangle the frame's mark used
     (5.6 on a side), centred in that area - 2.3 units of clearance above and
     below it, and 3.6 either side, so the tip sits clear of the base bar. Carries kb_text_hi (#FFF3EFE4) baked in. -->
